{"name":"Cabin Fever","hex":"#5e5349","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"cabin fever","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A condition of restlessness and irritability caused by being in a confined space.","Typhus."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/cabin_fever"}],"entries":[{"title":"B. M. Bower","blocks":[{"text":"Bertha Muzzy Sinclair or Sinclair-Cowan, née Muzzy, best known by her pseudonym B. M. Bower, was an American author who wrote novels, fictional short stories, and screenplays about the American Old West. Her works, featuring cowboys and cows of the Flying U Ranch in Montana, reflected \"an interest in ranch life, the use of working cowboys as main characters, the occasional appearance of eastern types for the sake of contrast, a sense of western geography as simultaneously harsh and grand, and a good deal of factual attention to such matters as cattle branding and bronc busting.\" She was married three times: to Clayton Bower in 1890, to Bertrand William Sinclair in 1905, and to Robert Elsworth Cowan in 1921. However, she chose to publish under the name Bower."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/8/8d/B._M._Bower.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/B._M._Bower"},{"title":"Cabin Fever (novel)","blocks":[{"text":"Cabin Fever (1990) is a novel by Australian writer Elizabeth Jolley. It was originally published by Viking in Australia in 1990."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/0/07/Cabin_Fever_%28novel%29_book_cover.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cabin_Fever_(novel)"},{"title":"Cabin Fever (2002 film)","blocks":[{"text":"Cabin Fever is a 2002 American comedy horror film, co-written and directed by Eli Roth in his directorial debut. It follows a group of college students who rent a cabin in the woods, where they unwittingly come in contact with an unknown flesh-eating disease. It stars Rider Strong, Jordan Ladd, James DeBello, Cerina Vincent, Joey Kern, and Giuseppe Andrews."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/7/71/Movie_poster_cabin_fever.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cabin_Fever_(2002_film)"},{"title":"Cabin fever","blocks":[{"text":"Cabin fever is the distressing irritability or restlessness experienced when a person, or group, is stuck at an isolated location or in confined quarters for an extended time. A person may be referred to as stir-crazy, derived from the use of stir meaning \"prison\"."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/20/CABIN%2C_INTERIOR%2C_LOOKING_SOUTHWEST_-_Roy_Fure%27s_Trapping_Cabin%2C_King_Salmon%2C_Bristol_Bay_Borough%2C_AK_HABS_AK%2C4-KISAL.V%2C1-5.tif/lossy-page1-330px-CABIN%2C_INTERIOR%2C_LOOKING_SOUTHWEST_-_Roy_Fure%27s_Trapping_Cabin%2C_King_Salmon%2C_Bristol_Bay_Borough%2C_AK_HABS_AK%2C4-KISAL.V%2C1-5.tif.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cabin_fever"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/e/e0/Eli_Roth.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled 1x","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/e/e0/Eli_Roth.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","alt":"Director Eli Roth in 2007","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AEli_Roth.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8e/Rider_Strong_2011_Shankbone.JPG/500px-Rider_Strong_2011_Shankbone.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8e/Rider_Strong_2011_Shankbone.JPG/1280px-Rider_Strong_2011_Shankbone.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_camp